{"book":24,"chapter":47,"context":{"chapter":47,"title":"The Sword Against Philistia","summary":"A flood from the north will overwhelm the Philistine cities of Gaza and Ashkelon; fathers flee without turning back for their children. The prophet begs the Lord's sword to rest in its sheath, but it cannot while it carries God's command.","background":"The Philistines held the southern coastal plain; Caphtor (v. 4), usually identified with Crete or the Aegean region, was remembered as their homeland (Amos 9:7). A Babylonian chronicle reports that Nebuchadnezzar sacked Ashkelon in 604 BC. The exact date of the Egyptian attack on Gaza (v. 1) is uncertain.","customs":[{"term":"How long wilt thou cut thyself?","verses":"47:5","note":"Shaving the head and gashing the body were mourning practices among Israel's neighbors, forbidden in Israel (Deuteronomy 14:1)."}],"watchFor":["Fathers too weak with fear to look back for their children (v. 3).","The prophet speaks to the sword itself (vv. 6–7)."],"connections":["Amos 9:7","Zephaniah 2:4-7","Ezekiel 25:15-17","Deuteronomy 14:1"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["דְבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] word of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["הַנָּבִיא","hanavi'","H5030","HTd/Ncmsa","the prophet"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","concerning"],["פְּלִשְׁתִּים","pelishtim","H6430","HNgmpa","[the] Philistines"],["בְּטֶרֶם","beterem","H2962","HR/Acbsa","<in> before"],["יַכֶּה","yakeh","H5221","HVhi3ms","he struck"],["פַרְעֹה","far'oh","H6547","HNcmsa","Pharaoh"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["עַזָּה","'azah","H5804","HNpl","Gaza"]],"x":[[24025020,24025020,5],[1010019,1010019,4],[2025015,2025017,3],[11004024,11004024,3],[38009005,38009007,3]],"xn":5},"2":{"w":[["כֹּה","koh","H3541","HD","thus"],["אָמַר","'amar","H559","HVqp3ms","he says"],["יְהוָה","yahweh",